Interactive USD edits of the camera parameters, with the render delegate

A grey sphere is rendered by a camera whose focal length, apertures, clipping range, projection and depth of field
are edited, the stage being re-rendered after each edit. The scenario only runs with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin
render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h: the procedural renders the
stage through an arnold camera made by the framework, that only follows the stage camera transform and field of view.
Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last render is compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't
rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
